{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610080659-redstone-workshop","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"industrial brick-and-timber workshop","rationale":"Second pass, judged as a person in the street would see it. Problems in the current build: (1) the office wing's tall stair roof towered over the east side and read as a ramp, so it becomes a low half-pitch dark-oak lean-to that rises from the east eave (y4.5) to the hall wall (y7.5) and leaves the hall's east clerestory visible; (2) the west and east faces were blank brick slabs, so they now carry recessed windows (glass set back 1 behind brick reveals), a dark-oak beam at the hood line (y6) and three posts on the west, which carries the frame around the corner as in the concept; (3) the parapet read as a grey stone box, so it becomes a brick parapet with a thin stone-brick slab cap sitting on a heavy dark-oak cornice that projects 1 on all sides, with upside-down stairs underneath, and the front posts poke above it as finials; (4) the front was a timber clutter, so it now has a clear three-bay rhythm: posts at x=0, 7 and 10 run from the plinth to the finial. The machine bay x1-6 y2-5 is fully open over a brick lean sill. The machine sits back on a smooth-stone bed with a lit redstone-lamp row on an andesite partition behind it, so the opening reads as a lit stage. A 2-deep dark-oak hood (with a stair-sloped top, stair brackets and two hanging lanterns) caps the opening. Above it a spruce sign board in a dark-oak frame is centred over the opening (x1-6, nudged from x3-6 so it is truly centred), with wall signs lying flat on the board; a projecting hanging sign would have stuck out sideways as a blade, so wall signs replace it. The iron-trapdoor louvres hang only over the solid bay 2 (x8-9), above its recessed tall pane window, following the rule that vents never sit over the opening. Office: window recessed with a fern in the reveal, door recessed 1 under a top-slab canopy, barrels beside it, and a corner post carrying the eave. The brick chimney is attached to the hall's east flank (x11-12, rather than freestanding at x13-14) and steps in by one block at the cornice, with a lit campfire on top. Andesite-wall stacks with polished-andesite caps stand on the flat roof, and an andesite duct drops from the cornice onto the office roof. Palette order kept: bricks dominant, dark oak frame, stone-brick plinth and kerb, grey andesite and iron accents, and red only from the machine."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:bricks","minecraft:stone_bricks","minecraft:cobblestone","minecraft:dark_oak_log","minecraft:dark_oak_planks","minecraft:dark_oak_stairs","minecraft:dark_oak_slab","minecraft:dark_oak_door","minecraft:spruce_planks","minecraft:dark_oak_wall_sign","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:iron_trapdoor","minecraft:andesite_wall","minecraft:polished_andesite","minecraft:stone_brick_slab","minecraft:smooth_stone","minecraft:hopper","minecraft:piston","minecraft:sticky_piston","minecraft:dispenser","minecraft:observer","minecraft:redstone_block","minecraft:redstone_wire","minecraft:redstone_torch","minecraft:repeater","minecraft:chest","minecraft:barrel","minecraft:redstone_lamp","minecraft:lantern","minecraft:campfire","minecraft:potted_fern","minecraft:stone"]},"placements":[{"op":"fill","from":[-2,0,-2],"to":[17,0,-1],"block":"minecraft:cobblestone"},{"op":"line","from":[-2,0,-2],"to":[17,0,-2],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,0,0],"to":[10,0,13],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[11,0,0],"to":[15,0,9],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[0,1,0],"to":[0,10,0],"block":"minecraft:bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[1,1,0],"to":[6,1,0],"block":"minecraft:bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[1,6,0],"to":[6,10,0],"block":"minecraft:bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[7,1,0],"to":[7,10,0],"block":"minecraft:bricks"},{"op":"fil